---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { absoluteUrl, isCommodityNode } from '../lib/site-variant';

if (!isCommodityNode) return Astro.redirect('/blog/');
const canonicalUrl = absoluteUrl('/plans/');
---

<Base
  title="Access"
  metaTitle="CommodityNode Access and Commercial Policy"
  description="What CommodityNode provides publicly, what professional capabilities are being validated, and why checkout remains disabled."
  canonicalUrl={canonicalUrl}
>
  <article class="static-page prose">
    <p class="section-label">Access</p>
    <h1>Public research is available. Professional access is not yet for sale.</h1>
    <p class="article-dek">
      CommodityNode does not put a price on an unfinished product or route a
      buyer into WorldMonitor billing. Checkout remains disabled until the
      advertised capability, legal, privacy, support, refund, and payment
      operations are independently verified.
    </p>

    <h2>Available now</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Published commodity research and evidence-backed Event Pulse pages.</li>
      <li>CommodityNode Live, benchmark tape, map, and three-hop published graph.</li>
      <li>Account-based saved commodities, companies, and routes.</li>
      <li>Deduplicated in-app alerts for new verified material Event Pulse and route updates.</li>
      <li>Read-only public graph endpoint and four MCP tools.</li>
      <li>Weekly brief double opt-in and custom exposure brief requests.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Professional candidate</h2>
    <p>
      The product contract under validation specifies ten years of historical
      replay, six-hop advanced paths, JSON/CSV/PNG graph export, and higher API
      quotas. These are acceptance targets, not currently purchasable features.
      No price is published.
    </p>

    <h2>What opens checkout</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Displayed product facts and limits match the runtime.</li>
      <li>Every paid feature passes end-to-end tests.</li>
      <li>Legal terms and the production privacy workflow are verified.</li>
      <li>A named operator owns support and refunds.</li>
      <li>Production payment webhooks and reconciliation pass.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>
      Organizations that need a decision-specific exposure analysis can request
      a scoped brief now. Intake does not imply acceptance, a subscription, or a
      promise of coverage.
    </p>
    <p>
      <a
        href="/brief/"
        data-commoditynode-event="pro_interest_opened"
        data-commoditynode-placement="plans_brief"
        data-commoditynode-conversion="pro"
      >Request a custom exposure brief</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</Base>
